-- title:
--   The history filtration of SAMBA
-- statement:
--   The **history** $\mathcal F_t$ at time $t$ is the $\sigma$-algebra generated by all the randomness used before time $t$: the arm uniforms $U_s$, the tie-break uniforms $V_s$ and the rewards $R_a(s)$ for $s<t$ and all arms $a$. The vectors $p(0),\dots,p(t)$ are determined by it, and it contains the paper's history $H(t-1)$ of arms played and rewards received before time $t$. The family $(\mathcal F_t)_{t\in\mathbb Z_+}$ is a filtration.
--
--   **Formalization Note** $\mathcal F_t$ also contains the tie-break variables and the rewards of arms that were not played. A Markov or supermartingale property with respect to $\mathcal F$ implies the same property for every smaller filtration to which the process is adapted.
-- source:
--   Denisov & Walton, Regret Analysis of a Markov Policy Gradient Algorithm for Multi-arm Bandits, arXiv:2007.10229v3, §3.2, p.7; §4.2, p.10

import Mathlib
import Definitions.Def_SambaPG_SambaNoise

open MeasureTheory

namespace SambaPG

/-- **The history filtration.**
Denisov & Walton, arXiv:2007.10229v3, §3.2, p.7 (the history `H(t)`) and §4.2, p.10.

`historyFiltration ξ t` is the σ-algebra generated by all the randomness used before time `t`: the
arm-drawing uniforms `U s`, the tie-breaking uniforms `V s` and the rewards `R_a(s)`, for `s < t`.
The SAMBA vector `p(t)` is measurable for it, and the paper's history `H(t − 1)` (arms played and
rewards received before `t`) is contained in it.

**Formalization Note.** The filtration also contains the tie-breaking variables and the rewards of
arms that were not played. A Markov or supermartingale property with respect to it implies the same
property with respect to any smaller filtration to which the process is adapted. -/
noncomputable def historyFiltration {A : Type*} [Fintype A] {B : BernoulliBandit A} {Ω : Type*}
    [MeasurableSpace Ω] {μ : Measure Ω} (ξ : SambaNoise B μ) : Filtration ℕ ‹MeasurableSpace Ω› where
  seq t := ⨆ (s : ℕ) (_ : s < t), ⨆ c : Src A,
    MeasurableSpace.comap (Src.coord ξ.U ξ.V ξ.R (s, c)) inferInstance
  mono' t₁ t₂ h := iSup₂_mono' fun s hs => ⟨s, lt_of_lt_of_le hs h, le_rfl⟩
  le' t := by
    refine iSup₂_le fun s _ => iSup_le fun c => ?_
    refine Measurable.comap_le ?_
    cases c with
    | arm => exact ξ.measurable_U s
    | tie => exact ξ.measurable_V s
    | reward a => exact ξ.measurable_R s a

end SambaPG


